05:22:29.981 --> 05:22:32.221
So the question is, how can we generate these videos

05:22:32.221 --> 05:22:34.081
and action controls for robots

05:22:34.431 --> 05:22:36.511
in a way that's guided by fine grained

05:22:36.511 --> 05:22:38.641
motions? So that

05:22:38.641 --> 05:22:40.981
takes us to our fourth last piece here,

05:22:41.141 --> 05:22:42.991
which is about motion guidance generation.

05:22:43.391 --> 05:22:45.491
If you look at the prior work,

05:22:46.371 --> 05:22:48.492
we see that standard

05:22:48.553 --> 05:22:51.031
text to video models struggle to generate

05:22:51.031 --> 05:22:52.471
these fine grained motions

05:22:53.431 --> 05:22:55.221
unless they are given explicit

05:22:55.680 --> 05:22:57.061
manual optical flow guidance.

05:22:58.922 --> 05:23:01.082
On the other hand, these VLA models, vision

05:23:01.082 --> 05:23:03.541
language action models, can control

05:23:03.680 --> 05:23:05.701
robots to perform tasks, but they

05:23:06.101 --> 05:23:08.261
require this massive expensive data

05:23:08.261 --> 05:23:10.181
set with robot demonstrations that are

05:23:10.582 --> 05:23:12.641
difficult to scale. So we're thinking about

05:23:12.641 --> 05:23:14.721
these two limitations and in this work, we

05:23:14.721 --> 05:23:16.431
try to tackle them by by

05:23:16.851 --> 05:23:18.931
first, removing the need to manually provide

05:23:18.931 --> 05:23:21.402
motion guidance and second,

05:23:22.101 --> 05:23:23.881
be able to to leverage Internet

05:23:24.181 --> 05:23:25.981
scale data for training.

05:23:26.231 --> 05:23:28.311
So how do we do that? Well, first, let's

05:23:28.311 --> 05:23:30.301
talk about how to remove

05:23:30.600 --> 05:23:32.801
the need to provide this manual

05:23:32.801 --> 05:23:34.461
guidance. So to tackle that first,

05:23:34.861 --> 05:23:36.941
issue, we actually proposed to generate the

05:23:36.941 --> 05:23:38.981
motion guidance automatically. So we

05:23:38.981 --> 05:23:41.241
can learn a model to generate that motion guidance

05:23:41.531 --> 05:23:43.471
than having a person to give it manually.

05:23:43.691 --> 05:23:45.641
So we call this, method

05:23:46.021 --> 05:23:48.041
Future Optical Flow Prediction of Offred

05:23:48.181 --> 05:23:50.201
and it converts those input visual

05:23:51.002 --> 05:23:53.082
observations and text into explicit motion

05:23:53.082 --> 05:23:55.401
representations, in pixel space.

05:23:56.361 --> 05:23:58.440
So looking a bit more closely, to

05:23:58.440 --> 05:24:00.241
do that, we basically

05:24:00.461 --> 05:24:02.619
use a latent diffusion model as a base

05:24:02.619 --> 05:24:04.811
architecture. But we train it to predict

05:24:04.811 --> 05:24:06.971
future motions. In the case

05:24:06.971 --> 05:24:08.991
of this paper, we choose a future

05:24:08.991 --> 05:24:11.110
optical flow as an explicit way to

05:24:11.110 --> 05:24:12.571
reason about the future motion.

05:24:13.451 --> 05:24:15.711
And we can train it using the usual diffusion

05:24:15.770 --> 05:24:17.971
loss, But an interesting

05:24:17.971 --> 05:24:20.131
key thing and people are if people are using,

05:24:20.451 --> 05:24:22.751
diffusion models to predict other

05:24:22.891 --> 05:24:25.311
than normal pixels or natural pixels,

05:24:25.529 --> 05:24:26.911
we found that it's easier

05:24:27.701 --> 05:24:30.041
